 (Song of Songs 1:2). Ba'al HaTurim applies that framework to Eve, reading the gematria of ויבאה as encoding these 24 adornments. The phrase 'adorn her with 24 adornments' specifically parallels language found in a baraita at Shabbat 88a. He then links the four Masorah occurrences of ויביאה to narratives of marital transition involving Pharaoh's daughter and Sarah's tent, themes developed in midrashic literature such as Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:2 and Bereshit Rabbah 60:16.", :sources ["Shabbat 88a" "Song of Songs 1:2" "Bereshit Rabbah 60:16" "Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויבאה", :a-value 24, :b "כ\"ד", :b-value 24, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["ויביאה אל האדם" "ויביאה יצחק האהלה" "ויביאה אל עיר דוד" "וישקוד ה' על הרעה ויביאה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויביאה אל האדם", :refs ["Genesis 2:22"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ויביאה יצחק האהלה", :refs ["Genesis 24:67"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ויביאה אל עיר דוד", :refs ["1 Kings 3:1"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וישקוד ה' על הרעה ויביאה", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:04:27.453795925Z", :model "glm-5.2"}